		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Medivh was the last Guardian of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}, the secret champion whom the wisest mages of the world empowered to stand against the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. He was the son of the Guardian {link:aegwynn}Aegwynn{/link} and of Nielas Aran, court conjurer of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. He was also the dearest friend of King {link:llane-wrynn}Llane Wrynn{/link} and of Sir {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link}. Yet the power that should have guarded {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} was poisoned before he drew his first breath, and it was Medivh who opened the way for the orcs to come.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[No mortal did more to bring about the age of war. Through Medivh, the demon lord {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} reached into the world and set the {link:horde}Horde{/link} upon the {link:humans}human{/link} kingdoms. The {link:first-war}First War{/link}, the fall of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} and every war that followed trace their roots to the tower where he lived.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "A Poisoned Birth",
			text = [=[{link:aegwynn}Aegwynn{/link} meant her son to be her heir, free of the council that had tried to rule her. She did not know that {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} had hidden his spirit within her since the day she struck down his avatar. When Medivh was conceived, the demon lord passed into the unborn child. The boy grew up bright and gentle, and he roamed the woods of the kingdom with {link:llane-wrynn}Llane{/link} and {link:anduin-lothar}Lothar{/link}. When he was fourteen, the power of the Guardian awoke within him, and with it the darkness that lay beneath. Medivh fell into a sleep that no healer could break. For years he lay in the care of the clerics of {link:northshire-abbey}Northshire Abbey{/link}. When he woke, he was a grown man, and he said nothing of what he had seen in the dark.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Karazhan",
			text = [=[Medivh made his home in {link:karazhan}Karazhan{/link}, a lonely tower in the land now called {link:deadwind-pass}Deadwind Pass{/link}. There, guided by the will that lived inside him, he reached across the void to a dying world called {red:draenor}Draenor{/red}. He found the {link:orcs}orc{/link} warlock {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link}, and together they opened the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}. The {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} sent him a young apprentice, {link:khadgar}Khadgar{/link}, who came to fear what he saw in the tower. The half-orc {link:garona}Garona{/link} also came to Karazhan as an envoy of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Through Khadgar and Garona, the truth at last reached {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He raised his power against the trolls of the south in his youth, at the side of {link:llane-wrynn}Llane{/link} and {link:anduin-lothar}Lothar{/link}.
• He opened the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} with {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} and the warlocks of Draenor.
• He took {link:khadgar}Khadgar{/link} as his apprentice and let him learn more than he meant to reveal.
• He watched from his tower as the {link:horde}Horde{/link} burned the kingdom of his oldest friends.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Fate",
			text = [=[{link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} and {link:khadgar}Khadgar{/link} climbed {link:karazhan}Karazhan{/link} to end the war at its root. With {link:garona}Garona{/link}'s help they confronted the Guardian, and there Medivh was slain. At the moment of his death, {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} tried to tear the secrets of the Tomb of {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} from his dying mind, and was cast into a long stupor for his pains. Medivh is dead. His tower stands empty and silent above {link:deadwind-pass}Deadwind Pass{/link}, and the folk of {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link} say that strange lights still burn in its windows.]=],
