		{
			title = "The Alliance",
			text = [=[When {link:anduin-lothar}Lothar{/link} brought the exiles of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} north, Terenas called the lords of the human nations to his capital. {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link}, {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link}, {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link}, {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link} and {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} sent their rulers and envoys, and the high elves of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} later joined them. Terenas gave Lothar command of the combined armies. {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}'s own lands suffered greatly in the war, yet in the end the {link:horde}Horde{/link} was broken, and its orcs were taken captive.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Fraying Peace",
			text = [=[After the war, Terenas ordered that the captured orcs be held in great internment camps. The camps were costly, and he taxed the other nations to pay for them. Quarrels grew over the camps and over the fate of the treacherous kingdom of {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link}. One by one, {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link}, {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link} and {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} withdrew from the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}. When a strange plague began to spread through the northern farmlands of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, the king sent his son {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} and the paladin {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther the Lightbringer{/link} to put an end to it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He welcomed the refugees of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} into his kingdom.
• He founded the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link} and gave {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} its command.
• He ordered the building of the internment camps after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.
• He sent {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} and {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther{/link} against the plague in the north.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Fate",
			text = [=[{link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} returned home from {red:northrend}Northrend{/red} as a hero, and the people of the capital strewed flower petals in his path. The prince walked into the throne room, knelt before his father, and then slew him with the runeblade {red:frostmourne}Frostmourne{/red}. With the king's death, the kingdom fell to the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther{/link} later carried the king's ashes in an urn toward {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, but Arthas struck down the paladin and cast the ashes aside. Terenas's capital lies in ruins, and beneath it the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} of Lady {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link} have built the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
	bonds = {
		{ id = "arthas-menethil", name = "Arthas Menethil", note = "his son, and his murderer" },
		{ id = "anduin-lothar", name = "Anduin Lothar", note = "commander of his Alliance" },
		{ id = "uther-the-lightbringer", name = "Uther the Lightbringer", note = "his loyal paladin" },
		{ id = "alonsus-faol", name = "Alonsus Faol", note = "archbishop of his faith" },
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "figure",
	id = "arthas-menethil",
	title = "Arthas Menethil",
