			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Gul'dan was the first {link:orcs}orc{/link} warlock and the architect of the old {link:horde}Horde{/link}. He was once the apprentice of the shaman {link:ner-zhul}Ner'zhul{/link}. He sold his people to the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} in exchange for power, and he poisoned both his race and his world. He opened the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} with {link:medivh}Medivh{/link} and led the Horde's hidden masters, the {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link}. In the end, he betrayed the Horde itself.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Much of the suffering of the orcs, and of the peoples they fought, can be traced to Gul'dan's ambition. His {link:fel-magic}fel magic{/link} drained the life from {red:draenor}Draenor{/red}. His demon blood made the orcs slaves to their rage. His betrayal cost the {link:horde}Horde{/link} the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Shadow Council",
			text = [=[On Draenor, the demon lord {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} sought a servant among the orcs. When {link:ner-zhul}Ner'zhul{/link} began to doubt the demon, Kil'jaeden turned to Gul'dan, who had no doubts at all. Kil'jaeden taught him the arts of fel sorcery. Gul'dan founded the {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link}, a circle of warlocks who ruled the clans from behind a puppet warchief, Blackhand. He offered the chieftains the blood of {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link}, and they drank. Then a voice from another world reached him. It was {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}, and together they opened the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Wars",
			text = [=[At the end of the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, Gul'dan tried to seize the secrets of the Tomb of {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} from {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}'s dying mind. The effort cast him into a long stupor. While he slept, {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link} killed Blackhand and destroyed most of the {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link}. When Gul'dan awoke, he bought his life with a promise of new weapons. He and his warlocks raised the first death knights of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Yet his loyalty was a mask. As Doomhammer besieged the capital of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, Gul'dan took his followers and sailed away to seek the Tomb of Sargeras beneath the sea.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He founded the {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link} and ruled the {link:horde}Horde{/link} through Blackhand.
• He gave the chieftains the blood of {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link}.
• He opened the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} with {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}.
• He raised the first death knights of the Horde.
• He abandoned Doomhammer at the gates of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}'s capital.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Fate",
			text = [=[Gul'dan raised the Tomb of {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} from the depths of the Great Sea and entered it, hoping to claim the power of a god. The demons who guarded it tore him to pieces. Doomhammer's warriors, sent to punish his treachery, slaughtered his followers. Without them, the {link:horde}Horde{/link} could not hold the siege, and it was driven back into defeat. Gul'dan's skull survived him, and it carried dark power of its own until it was destroyed in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
