	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Ner'zhul was the elder shaman of the Shadowmoon clan and the most respected spiritual leader of the orcs of {red:draenor}Draenor{/red}. The demon lord {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} deceived him and used him to turn the orcs against the draenei. Later, Ner'zhul tore his own world apart in an attempt to flee it. Captured by the demons, he was made into the {red:lich-king}Lich King{/red}, master of the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Ner'zhul brought ruin twice. As a shaman, he opened his people's hearts to the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. As the Lich King, he sent a plague of undeath upon {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. The {link:third-war}Third War{/link} and the dead lands of the north are his work as much as any other's.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Deceiver",
			text = [=[In the old days of Draenor, the orcs lived as clans of hunters and shamans. Ner'zhul spoke for the spirits among them. Then {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} came to him, disguised as a spirit of the ancestors, and whispered that the peaceful draenei were plotting against the orcs. Ner'zhul believed him and led his people into war. Only later did he see the truth, and when he refused to go further, Kil'jaeden turned to his apprentice, {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link}, instead. Ner'zhul was cast aside and lived in shame while the {link:horde}Horde{/link} marched to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Shattering",
			text = [=[After the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the orcs who had stayed on Draenor gathered around the old shaman. He reopened the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} and sent warriors to steal powerful relics from {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, meaning to open gateways to new worlds for his people. The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} sent an expedition through the Portal to stop him. Ner'zhul opened his gateways anyway. The energies tore Draenor apart, and he fled through a rift with his followers.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He led the orcs as their greatest shaman.
• He led the clans against the draenei under {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link}'s deception.
• He reopened the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.
• He shattered Draenor with his gateways.
• As the Lich King, he raised the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} and loosed the plague upon {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Fate",
			text = [=[{link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} was waiting for him beyond the rift. The demon tore the flesh from the shaman's body and bound his spirit in a suit of armor and a helm. He sealed Ner'zhul in a block of ice and hurled it to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. It fell on the glacier of Icecrown in {red:northrend}Northrend{/red}, and there he became the Lich King. From the Frozen Throne he raised the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. He called {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link} to his service and sent the plague south. At last he claimed the prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} through the runeblade {red:frostmourne}Frostmourne{/red}. When his power waned, he summoned Arthas to Icecrown, and the prince put on his helm. Ner'zhul and Arthas are now one, and the Lich King rules in the north.]=],
		},
	},
	bonds = {
