			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Illidan Stormrage was a {link:night-elves}night elf{/link} sorcerer of the ancient world, the twin brother of {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link} and a rival for the love of {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link}. He fought the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}, and he also served it. He was imprisoned for ten thousand years and freed in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}. Some call him a hero and many call him a traitor. His own people named him the Betrayer.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Illidan's choices have saved and threatened the world in equal measure. In ancient times, he carried the waters of the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} to {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}, where they still lie beneath {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, he slew a lord of the Legion and took its power for himself.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The War of the Ancients",
			text = [=[Illidan was born with amber eyes, a mark said to foretell greatness. He was drawn to {link:arcane-magic}arcane magic{/link} as his brother was drawn to the path of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}. In the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, he fought beside the night elves against {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link} and her demon allies. Yet he grew jealous of his brother and hungry for power, and he went at last to {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} himself. The demon lord burned away his eyes and gave him a new sight. When the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} was destroyed, Illidan poured stolen vials of its water into a lake atop {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}, creating a new Well. {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion{/link} judged this a crime. He had his brother chained beneath the earth, guarded by the warden Maiev Shadowsong.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Third War",
			text = [=[Ten thousand years later, the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} and the Legion came to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. Against her people's law, {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande{/link} freed Illidan to help. In the forest now called {link:felwood}Felwood{/link}, he consumed the Skull of {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link}, took on the shape of a demon, and slew the dreadlord {link:tichondrius}Tichondrius{/link}. {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion{/link} banished him from the forests of the night elves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He fought against {link:azshara}Azshara{/link} in the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}.
• He created a new {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} atop {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}.
• He consumed the {link:skull-of-gul-dan}Skull of Gul'dan{/link} and slew {link:tichondrius}Tichondrius{/link}.
• He raised the {link:naga}naga{/link} of the depths to serve him after the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Fate",
			text = [=[After his banishment, Illidan gathered the {link:naga}Naga{/link} and sought the Tomb of {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} beneath the sea. He was pursued by Maiev, and by his brother and {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande{/link}, and he escaped them all. Later he marched on {red:northrend}Northrend{/red} to strike at the {red:lich-king}Lich King{/red}. At the glacier of Icecrown, he fought {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} and was defeated. He fled with his surviving followers. Where he went after that, no chronicle of the kingdoms can say.]=],
