			text = [=[Every war the Legion has waged on {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} has been waged in Sargeras's name. He reached the world three times: through {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link}, through {link:aegwynn}Aegwynn{/link} and her son {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}, and through the orcs he bound to his will. His shadow lies behind the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, the {link:first-war}First War{/link} and the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Fallen Titan",
			text = [=[The histories say that Sargeras hunted demons across the Great Dark for longer than any mortal can reckon. What he saw there turned his heart. He came to believe that creation itself was flawed and could not be mended. He set free the demons he had caught, and he corrupted the eredar through {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} and {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link}, and so the Legion was born.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Azeroth",
			text = [=[Ten thousand years ago, {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link} and her Highborne drew his eye with the power of the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}. Sargeras sent his Legion through their portal, and he sought to enter the world himself. The Well was destroyed before he could. Ages later, he appeared before the Guardian {link:aegwynn}Aegwynn{/link} in a great storm in {red:northrend}Northrend{/red}. She slew his avatar and sealed its body in a tomb beneath the sea. His spirit hid within her and passed into her unborn son. Through {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}, the dark titan opened the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} and brought the orcs to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}.]=],
